.Dd February 28, 2026
.Dt ELFEDIT 1
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm elfedit
.Nd edit ELF metadata fields safely with validation controls
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl f
.Op Fl n
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl -input-mmap
.Op Fl o Ar output
.Op Fl -output-type Ns = Ns Ar type
.Op Fl -output-machine Ns = Ns Ar machine
.Op Fl -output-osabi Ns = Ns Ar osabi
.Op Fl -output-abiversion Ns = Ns Ar version
.Op Fl -output-flags Ns = Ns Ar flags
.Op Fl -output-entry Ns = Ns Ar address
.Op Fl -set-section-type Ar name Ns = Ns Ar type
.Op Fl -set-section-flags Ar name Ns = Ns Ar flags
.Op Fl -set-section-align Ar name Ns = Ns Ar align
.Op Fl -rename-section Ar old Ns = Ns Ar new
.Op Fl -set-segment-type Ar idx Ns = Ns Ar type
.Op Fl -set-segment-flags Ar idx Ns = Ns Ar flags
.Op Fl -set-segment-align Ar idx Ns = Ns Ar align
.Ar input
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
opens an ELF file, applies requested metadata edits through
.Xr libelfobj 3 ,
runs strict validation, and writes the result either in-place or to
an alternate path.
In-place updates are written through a temporary file and then renamed over the
original.
.Pp
Without
.Fl f ,
strict validation failures prevent writing.
With
.Fl n ,
all edits and validation run but no file is written.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--output-abiversion"
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Write output even when strict validation fails.
Prints:
.Dq WARNING: writing structurally invalid ELF .
.It Fl n , Fl -dry-run
Apply edits and run validation but do not write output.
Exit status is 0 when validation passes and 1 when validation fails.
.It Fl v , Fl -verbose
Print each field mutation as it is applied.
.It Fl -input-mmap
Hint to use memory-mapped input for parsing.
.It Fl o Ar file , Fl -output Ns = Ns Ar file
Write to a separate output path instead of in-place replacement.
.It Fl V , Fl -version
Print
.Nm
version information.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print command usage.
.El
.Sh HEADER EDIT VALUES
.Ss "--output-type"
.Bl -column "name" "value"
.It Sy name Ta Sy value
.It none Ta 0
.It rel Ta 1
.It exec Ta 2
.It dyn Ta 3
.It core Ta 4
.El
.Pp
Numeric values are also accepted.
.Ss "--output-machine"
.Bl -column "name" "value"
.It Sy name Ta Sy value
.It i386 Ta 3
.It x86_64 Ta 62
.It x86-64 Ta 62
.It arm Ta 40
.It aarch64 Ta 183
.It mips Ta 8
.It riscv Ta 243
.El
.Pp
Numeric values are also accepted.
.Ss "--output-osabi"
.Bl -column "name" "value"
.It Sy name Ta Sy value
.It none Ta 0
.It sysv Ta 0
.It linux Ta 3
.It freebsd Ta 9
.It substrate Ta 64
.El
.Pp
Numeric values in the range 0-255 are also accepted.
.Sh EDIT OPERATIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--set-section-flags"
.It Fl -output-abiversion Ns = Ns Ar version
Set
.Va EI_ABIVERSION
(0-255).
.It Fl -output-flags Ns = Ns Ar flags
Set ELF header
.Va e_flags
(decimal or hexadecimal).
.It Fl -output-entry Ns = Ns Ar address
Set ELF header
.Va e_entry
(decimal or hexadecimal).
.It Fl -set-section-type Ar name Ns = Ns Ar type
Set
.Va sh_type
for section
.Ar name .
Types accepted:
.Dq progbits ,
.Dq nobits ,
.Dq note ,
.Dq symtab ,
.Dq strtab ,
.Dq rela ,
.Dq rel ,
.Dq dynamic ,
.Dq hash ,
or numeric.
.It Fl -set-section-flags Ar name Ns = Ns Ar flags
Set
.Va sh_flags
for section
.Ar name .
Accepts either a hexadecimal/decimal number or a comma-separated list:
.Dq alloc ,
.Dq write ,
.Dq execinstr ,
.Dq merge ,
.Dq strings ,
.Dq tls ,
.Dq group ,
.Dq compressed .
.It Fl -set-section-align Ar name Ns = Ns Ar align
Set
.Va sh_addralign
for section
.Ar name .
.It Fl -rename-section Ar old Ns = Ns Ar new
Rename a section in
.Pa .shstrtab .
.It Fl -set-segment-type Ar idx Ns = Ns Ar type
Set program header
.Va p_type
at index
.Ar idx .
Named values include
.Dq null ,
.Dq load ,
.Dq dynamic ,
.Dq interp ,
.Dq note ,
.Dq phdr ,
.Dq tls ,
or numeric.
.It Fl -set-segment-flags Ar idx Ns = Ns Ar flags
Set program header
.Va p_flags
at index
.Ar idx .
Accepts
.Dq r ,
.Dq w ,
.Dq x
combos (e.g. rwx) or numeric.
.It Fl -set-segment-align Ar idx Ns = Ns Ar align
Set program header
.Va p_align
at index
.Ar idx .
Segment payload bytes are not rewritten; these are metadata edits.
.El
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
Common failures include:
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Dq elfedit: <file>: not an ELF file
.It
.Dq elfedit: unknown type: <value>
or equivalent machine/osabi errors
.It
.Dq elfedit: section '<name>' not found
.It
.Dq elfedit: segment index <N> out of range (0-<max>)
.It
strict validation diagnostics from
.Xr elf_validate 3
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr readelf 1 ,
.Xr libelfobj 3 ,
.Xr elf_validate 3
